Create a .cc file
Throw all of the Pythia code in the file
To compile this C++ file and be able to use ROOT library features:
  g++ -I/home/ajrosy/pythia8317/include eventgen.cc -o eventgen -lpythia8 -L/home/ajrosy/pythia8317/lib $(root-config --cflags --libs)
  export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=${LD_LIBRARY_PATH}:/home/ajrosy/pythia8317/lib
  ./filename

To send results to an output file:
  ./filename > output.out

----------------------------------------------------------------
Useful Pythia commands:

#include "Pythia.h"
#include <TCanvas.h>
using namespace Pythia8;

int main() {
  Pythia pythia;
  pythia.readString("Beams:eCM = 100.");
  pythia.readString("another specification");
  pythia.init();

  pythia.next();
  return 0;
}

----------------------------------------------------------------
PYTHIA has this subprocess:    gamma q -> q g (udscb)  with code number 284  and with estimated max cross section 6.814e-07 mb
  Maybe focus on this?  It describes the electron emitting a virtual photon that interacts with one of the quarks of the proton.  This creates a quark and gluon, which can become jets.
